<script>
  /* Bottomdescription "Read More" toggle. Inline <script> runs synchronously during
     HTML parsing — but theme.liquid loads jQuery with `defer`, so `jQuery` is not yet
     defined here. Wrap in DOMContentLoaded (defer scripts finish before DCL fires)
     so jQuery is guaranteed loaded by the time we run.
     Scoped to .bottomdescription so any other .readmore-text on the page is not affected.
     Idempotent: short-circuits if a .readMore is already next-sibling (defends against
     shopify:section:load re-runs and double-bind). */
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function () {
    if (typeof jQuery === 'undefined') return;
    var $ = jQuery;
    var $rmText = $('.bottomdescription .readmore-text');
    if (!$rmText.length || $rmText.next('.readMore').length) return;
    $rmText.hide();
    $rmText.after('<a class="readMore" style="cursor:pointer;margin-top:12px;margin-bottom:12px;display:inline-block;background:#5b1129;color:#ffffff;padding:5px 15px;">Read More</a>');
    $('.bottomdescription').off('click.readmore').on('click.readmore', '.readMore', function () {
      var $btn = $(this);
      $btn.prev('.readmore-text').slideToggle(200, function () {
        $btn.text($btn.text() === 'Read More' ? 'Close' : 'Read More');
      });
      return false;
    });
  });
</script>

{%- comment -%}
  Variant picker + AJAX Add to cart is handled by the shared global
  assets/ona-product-card.js (loaded unconditionally in layout/theme.liquid),
  not by rendering ona-product-card-atc.liquid here. That snippet's inline
  script predates the native-radio-input card markup ona-product-card.liquid
  now uses ([data-card-variant] radio + [data-card-pill] <label for="...">)
  -- its click handler on [data-card-pill] called e.preventDefault(), which
  suppressed the label's native "check the associated radio" behavior, so
  the radio's checked state never changed and ona-product-card.js's
  change-event listener never fired. The stale script then set the Add to
  cart button to "Sold out" itself, reading data-variant-* attributes off
  the label that don't exist there anymore (they live on the sibling radio
  input) -- so every variant selection showed the button as sold out
  regardless of real availability. ona-product-recommendations.liquid was
  already migrated off this render call for the same reason; this was the
  one remaining call site.
{%- endcomment -%}

